      id: "r09", date: "2026-09-25", theme: "社会现象", level: "四级",
      title: "Living with Social Media: Connection or Illusion?",
      text: "For most college students today, social media is not a hobby but a background of daily life. They wake up with it, walk to class with it, and fall asleep with it. There is no doubt that these platforms bring real benefits. Students far from home can see their families at any moment, share study notes with classmates, and follow lectures and ideas from all over the world. However, a growing number of researchers warn that frequent use may create a strange feeling of being busy yet lonely. One explanation is that online interaction is often shallow. Liking a post takes a second, but it does not carry the warmth of a real conversation. Another explanation concerns comparison. Because people usually post only the happiest moments of their lives, users may wrongly believe that everyone else is more successful and more popular than they are, which slowly damages confidence. Some students report that the more time they spend scrolling, the harder it becomes to concentrate on a book for even twenty minutes. Teachers and psychologists give similar advice rather than demanding that students quit social media completely. They suggest setting clear boundaries, such as keeping phones out of the bedroom, turning off unnecessary notifications, and choosing one or two moments a day to check messages on purpose. The goal, they say, is not to reject technology but to use it as a tool instead of being used by it. A student who follows this advice described the change simply: I did not lose my friends online; I just got my attention back.",
      trans: "对今天大多数大学生来说，社交媒体不是爱好，而是日常生活的背景。醒来时带着它，走去上课时带着它，睡觉时也带着它。毫无疑问，这些平台带来真实的好处：离家在外的学生随时能看到家人、与同学分享笔记、关注来自世界各地的讲座和观点。然而，越来越多研究者警告，频繁使用可能造成一种奇怪的感觉——很忙却孤独。一种解释是线上互动往往很浅：点赞只需一秒，却承载不了真实交谈的温度。另一种解释与比较有关：由于人们通常只发布生活中最快乐的时刻，用户可能误以为别人都比自己更成功、更受欢迎，这会慢慢损害自信。一些学生表示，刷手机越久，就越难连续二十分钟专注读书。教师和心理学家的建议并非要求彻底戒掉社交媒体，而是设定清晰边界：把手机留在卧室之外、关闭不必要的通知、每天有意识地选一两个固定时段查看消息。他们说，目标不是拒绝技术，而是把它当作工具，而不是被它使用。一位照此做的学生这样总结变化：我并没有失去网上的朋友，我只是把注意力拿回来了。",
